    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d816">

                <pb facs="0816" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg712"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6177.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-15T22:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1913—10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Please call the attention of the President to the circumstance that the
                    Associated Press has brought a [rumor?] to Mexico that the President has stated
                    that he would intervene in Mexico only after a wanton slaughter of Americans.
                    The Mexican Herald suppressed this telegram, but President Madero used it today
                    in connection with his arguments why he should not resign.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
